{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"2503 AMEND WORK COMPLETE (uncommitted, awaiting the stacked rebase).\nParity is now scoped by library_symbol rather than correspondence, so every tool with a counterpart\nis checked; mcp_only (null symbol) unchanged. _facade_function now RAISES naming the symbol and what\nthe attribute is actually bound to, instead of silently returning the stand-in and reporting parity\nit never verified.\nOracle 25/25. make lint exit 0. criteria-vocabulary 48 passed, confirming my synthetic-repo stub.\n\nTHE FIVE co_names DIVERGENCES ARE ALL DELIBERATE — the agent verified each at its call site rather\nthan writing a plausible reason:\n comment_ticket   allow_secret_pattern is 'Deliberately not exposed over MCP' per rebar.comment's own\n                  docstring (bug e7a9) — an MCP caller must not be able to suppress the write-time\n                  secret screen;  is importer-only provenance.\n create_idea      the tool PINS return_alias=True and _creation_channel='mcp' at the call site.\n log_session      pins _creation_channel='mcp' so an MCP-written log's provenance cannot be spoofed.\n transition_ticket exposes only the current ; force_close is a DEPRECATED alias that warns and\n                  maps onto it. Reason notes the declaration will go STALE if the alias is removed.\n ready_tickets    MCP-only , implemented in the MCP layer for the payload budget.\n\nJUDGMENT CALL I WAS ASKED TO MAKE, AND MY RULING: the agent flagged ready_tickets/full as the nearest\nthing to real drift and invited me to overrule, since the lean-vs-full concept exists on\nrebar.list_tickets and rebar.search but not rebar.ready. ACCEPTED AS A DECLARED DIVERGENCE, not\ndrift: the seam's own docstring states rebar.ready carries no such flag and 'this change deliberately\nadds none', and the projection routes through the shared lean_projection that list_tickets uses, so\nthe two discovery surfaces cannot disagree. It is a transport concern the library does not have.\nRecording the reasoning because a later reader may reasonably revisit it.\n\nDISCIPLINE WORTH NOTING: the agent refused to call the full unit tier green while its run was still\nin flight, and said so rather than reporting a result it did not have. That is exactly the failure\nmode that produced the 2503 CI red — I had reported green off targeted tests only.\nOrphan check clean: python scripts/check_orphaned_load.py reports nothing, so no agent left a\nbackground pytest reparented to PID 1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788322967768068001,"uuid":"71663033-b3c0-4d3e-b342-f78a352f613e"}